  "body": "Noted by the high-tier review of PR #1140 (review comment on that PR, head 68d317b7), merged today on the maintainer's word.\n\nSetting the environment variable `CAMCRAFT_CARRY_ENGINE=field` makes a shipped build carry machined stock between setups on the field engine, not the default column engine. Nothing on it passes silently, but it behaves differently from the default: it refuses cylinder stock, and it reports a different gouge depth for the same program. An environment variable is invisible in the project and in the UI, so two machines can judge the same file differently without anyone knowing why.\n\nSuggested (reviewer): limit the switch to test builds (`cfg(test)` / a cargo feature) until #589 makes the field engine the default; or, if it must stay reachable, say which engine judged in the verdict text and the setup sheet.\n\nDone means: a release build ignores the variable (or names the engine in every verdict it produces), pinned by a test; the engine-agreement lane keeps its own way to select the field engine.",
